# Begin a mapping run: move pgo_node from IDLE to MAPPING.
#
# Served by pgo_node (`syncai_mapping`, in SyncAI-Robot-Workspace) on the
# relative name `start_mapping`, so it lands on <robot_id>/pgo/start_mapping.
# The backend is its only caller (the console's "Start mapping" control).
# Added 2026-10 together with msg/MappingStatus.msg, when pgo gained an
# explicit idle state: until then the mapping session began building a graph
# the moment pointlio published, so the drive from wherever the robot was
# powered on to the site's starting point was already part of the map, and
# the only way to end a run was to tear the session down.
#
# Same sequence as ResetMapping, with a different precondition: pause intake,
# reset the LIO front end over ResetLIO (reset_lio true), build a fresh pose
# graph, resume behind a timestamp gate that drops the old stream's tail.
# "Begin a clean run from where the robot stands now" is literally true only
# with reset_lio: the pose graph's origin is the odometry origin, and a LIO
# reset puts that at the robot's current pose with a fresh gravity alignment.
#
# Refused (success false, nothing touched) when pgo is already MAPPING -- use
# reset_mapping to start over, or save_maps to finish -- and while another
# start or reset is in flight. A failed ResetLIO round trip leaves pgo IDLE.
# A successful save_maps is what brings pgo back to IDLE, so the run is
# bracketed: start_mapping ... save_maps, then start_mapping again.
#
# THE ROBOT MUST BE STANDING STILL when reset_lio is true, from the call until
# pointlio has re-initialised (a few seconds; it publishes nothing meanwhile,
# so the live scan goes dark and comes back). See ResetLIO.srv. Nothing in
# either node enforces it.

# Reset the LIO front end first -- what the console sends. False begins a
# graph over the running odometry stream: the origin is then wherever pointlio
# was launched, not where the robot stands. A bag-replay affordance.
bool reset_lio
---
bool success
# Rendered verbatim by the operator console, so pgo writes it as UI copy
# (including the stillness warning) rather than as a log line.
string message

# pointlio's last published odometry stamp, echoed for log correlation. 0.0
# when reset_lio was false or the front end had not reached MAPPING. Pairs
# stamped at or before it are the old stream's tail and are dropped.
float64 lio_last_odom_time
